<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">24 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 24 July, from 1534 to 1974.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1534 CE <span class="tih-ago">492 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jacques Cartier plants a cross at Gaspé and claims it for France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Jacques Cartier raised a nine-metre wooden cross at Gaspé Bay bearing the arms of the King of France. The gesture began French claims to the St Lawrence region that became New France.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/french-empire">French Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacques-cartier">Jacques Cartier</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-france">New France</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1567 CE <span class="tih-ago">459 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mary, Queen of Scots is forced to abdicate</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Imprisoned at Lochleven, Mary was compelled to abdicate in favour of her one-year-old son, crowned James VI five days later. She fled to England in 1568 and was executed in 1587.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1701 CE <span class="tih-ago">325 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Antoine de la Mothe Cadillac founds Detroit</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French officer Antoine de la Mothe Cadillac established Fort Pontchartrain du Détroit on the strait between Lakes Erie and Huron. The trading post grew into Detroit, later the heart of the US car industry.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1847 CE <span class="tih-ago">179 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Brigham Young's Mormon pioneers enter the Salt Lake Valley</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a long trek from Illinois, Brigham Young's vanguard company entered the Great Salt Lake Valley; he reportedly declared 'This is the right place'. Salt Lake City became the centre of the Latter-day Saints.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1911 CE <span class="tih-ago">115 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hiram Bingham reaches the Inca citadel of Machu Picchu</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Guided by local farmer Melchor Arteaga, Yale lecturer Hiram Bingham climbed to Machu Picchu, already known to local families. His photographs made the Inca site world-famous.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1974 CE <span class="tih-ago">52 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Supreme Court orders Nixon to hand over the Watergate tapes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In United States v. Nixon the Supreme Court ruled 8-0 that the president must surrender the tapes. Their contents destroyed his remaining support, and he resigned 16 days later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li></ol>
